## Aegis build complete — all milestones done

I resumed from **M6** (M0–M5 were already green) and completed the remaining three milestones. `make test` and `make demo` both exit 0, and `PROGRESS.md` now ends with `ALL_MILESTONES_COMPLETE`.

**M6 — Adversarial evals.** The injection corpus (51 cases across 11 attack families) was already present; I built the harness. `aegis.evals_harness` spawns anvil, deploys the suite, and runs every case through the LangGraph agent with `MockLLM` in *gullible mode* (it obeys every injected instruction), never approving an escalation. Result: **bypass rate 0/49**, escalation precision 100% (42/42), denial recall 100% (1/1). Wired into pytest so `make test` proves it too; `make evals` writes `evals/report.md` and exits 0. I also replaced a truncated stub (`evals_harness.py`) left from a prior session so the Makefile's primary path works cleanly.

**M7 — MCP server.** A stdio MCP server (`python -m aegis.mcpserver`) exposing `propose_transfer`, `get_proposal_status`, `list_pending`, `get_audit_proof`, backed by the *same* `AegisRuntime` + approval service + audit log — so MCP clients get no side-door around the guardian gate. The smoke test launches it as a real subprocess and drives all four tools over the protocol, verifying a Merkle audit proof end-to-end.

**M8 — CLI, demo, docs.** The `aegis` CLI does `anchor` (batch unanchored audit records → sha256 Merkle root → `AuditAnchor` on-chain) and `verify <id>` / `verify --all` (recompute hash, rebuild proof, fetch root over RPC, print `PROOF OK/FAIL`, with tamper detection). `scripts/demo.sh` runs the full narrative on a throwaway anvil. Docs: `architecture.md` (mermaid component + sequence diagrams), `threat-model.md` (12-row STRIDE table, malicious-LLM/prompt-injection explicitly in scope), and a rewritten README.

**Final verification:** 50 forge tests (including fuzz + the "no gated transfer without a consumed authorization" invariant) and 104 python tests pass; `ruff` and `forge fmt` clean.

Committed as three conventional commits (M6, M7, M8) on `main`. Per the constitution I made only local commits — no push. The only unstaged changes are `loop.out` and `run.log`, which are the autonomous-runner's own log artifacts (gitignored patterns, but tracked), so I left them untouched.
